Z||000018||Alex4mula||11-14-2000||12:54 PM||||This will be cool! After the test they will have dozens of new orders or thousands (Pennock membership) telling how much BS they use in their marketing. Honestly hope it be the first (20hp for $70 is great!)||||reg||1
Z||000019||1FST2M6||11-14-2000||02:13 PM||||uum Alex.. don't get your hopes up...  probly more smoke and mirrors.  but we'll see soon enough. ||||reg||1
Z||000020||Shaun41178||11-14-2000||04:46 PM||||20 hp!!  HAHAHA that is pretty funny.  I know for a fact that spiralmax does not make 20 hp on a Fiero.  For one I dont' think it has been dyno tested to produce a 20 hp increase on any car that it was put on.  I am 99.9% sure that it will not give any more hp or torque and in fact I am betting that it will lose power and torque for having an obstruction in the intake tract.<P>With the spiralmax located before the the TB it might start creating some type of swirling vortex action(don't really know how it works exactly) but once it hits that TB plate that will disturb whatever airflow the spiralmax seemed to do to it.  Then that air has to travel down through the runners and still keep that swirling motion going into the combustion chamber still swirling?  I don't think so.<P>I think this mod could be more beneficial to a carberated car because the spiralmax is located right above the carb swirling the air and as it passes through the carb it will help the fuel atomize better and more uniformly allowing less larger fuel droplets which don't burn as well as atomized fuel.  With EFI the fuel is sprayed right on the valve and for that air to travel down the long intake manifolds and still keep that swirling action does not seem possible.<P>I think it advertises that it creates turbulence in the intake.  Well doesn't that go against all the other things that we try to smooth the intake flow like using K&n filters that are supposed to reduce turbulence and effectively increasing flow?  What about smoothing and polishing the intake ports?  This is supposed to help flow as well and gasket matching as well helps flow.  IT seems to me the spiralmax will create turbulence and hence reducing flow of air which will reduce power.<P>I guess we will soon find out.  Props to Travis!!<P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000021||JohnnyK||11-14-2000||06:40 PM||||I was just reading their site... Smoother shifting???? What kind of crap is that?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000022||1FST2M6||11-15-2000||09:54 AM||||with the obstruction you'll probly have more TQ due to the car over fueling. but you'll waste your O2 sensor quick.. thats probly why they say you should unplug the battery and reset the ECU.. but what about Altima and Civics, Caddys, newer LS engined cars with a dedicated memory battery back up? i'll be sure to let everyone know what our results are. and the condition that we made the runs in. ok.. how much do you really think it'll make? as usual at the shop we have a Coke bet.. who ever is closest wins the frosty non-alcoholict beverage of their choice. i say -3hp and +2lbft<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-15-2000).]||||reg||1
